    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. It splits into three stages: **Bean-Validation on the request body** (before the controller runs), **mapper normalizations**, then **the service-layer checks and side-effects**.\n\n## Stage A \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body (`@Valid OwnerFieldsDto`)\nFailure of any of these \u2192 HTTP **400** (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`). No custom `@InitBinder`/`Validator` exists; these are all annotation constraints.\n\n1. **firstName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, allowing up to two space/apostrophe/hyphen-separated parts).\n2. **lastName** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, with optional trailing `.`).\n3. **address** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank).\n4. **city** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern(\".*\\S.*\")` (non-blank).\n5. **telephone** \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, and custom `@TelephoneDigits` (must normalize to valid E.164 via `TelephoneNormalizer`: 8\u201315 digits, `+61` assumed if no `+`, per-country length check).\n6. **email** \u2014 `@Email`, `@Size(max=255)`; nullable.\n7. **postcode** \u2014 `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{4}$\")`; nullable.\n8. **registrationDate** \u2014 `@PastOrPresent`; nullable.\n9. **birthDate** \u2014 no value constraint (just date-format binding); nullable.\n10. **Class-level `@ValidPostcodeForCity`** (cross-field) \u2014 a well-formed postcode must match the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099; unknown regions accepted). Violation attached to the `postcode` field.\n\nAlso enforced before the method body: `@PreAuthorize(hasRole(OWNER_ADMIN))` \u2014 Spring Security (403 if unauthorized).\n\n## Stage B \u2014 Mapper normalizations (`ownerMapper.toOwner`, before the service)\nThese mutate the values that get persisted:\n\n11. **address** \u2192 normalized (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand ST\u2192STREET, RD\u2192ROAD, AVE\u2192AVENUE).\n12. **telephone** \u2192 converted to canonical E.164.\n13. **email** \u2192 lower-cased (null-safe).\n14. `id` and `pets` deliberately ignored; other fields copied as-is. `sharesHousehold` is read separately in the controller (not persisted).\n\n## Stage C \u2014 Service `createOwner(owner, sharesHousehold)` (`@Transactional`) \u2014 checks and side-effects, in exact order\nNote that some of these are **validations** (throw) and some are **side-effects/field mutations**, interleaved:\n\n15. **Disposable-email check** \u2192 `DisposableEmailDomainException` (**400**) if the domain is on the blocklist (mailinator/tempmail/guerrillamail).\n16. **Side-effect:** set `householdId` = SHA-256-derived hash of `lastName|postcode`.\n17. **Identity-collision check** (`findByTelephone`, compares telephone|email|householdId) \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerException` (**409**).\n18. **Household-duplicate check** (`findByLastNameIgnoreCase`, same householdId): if members exist and `sharesHousehold` is false \u2192 `HouseholdDuplicateException` (**409**). (Skipped when postcode is null.)\n19. **City-capacity check** (`countByCity`): if `>= 50` \u2192 `CityCapacityExceededException` (**409**).\n20. **Side-effect:** default `registrationDate` to today if null, then adjust weekends forward to the next business day (`BusinessDayAdjuster`).\n21. **Daily-limit check** (`countByRegistrationDate`): if `>= 100` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (**429**).\n22. **Side-effect:** set `bulkSignupWarning = true` if that day's existing count `> 80`.\n23. **Side-effect:** `flagPossibleDuplicate` \u2014 if not sharing household, set `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf` from a household member with a different telephone.\n24. **Side-effect:** set `namesakeCount` (same last name + same first name, case-insensitive).\n25. **Side-effect:** set `householdSize` = household members + 1.\n26. **Side-effect:** set `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region resolved from postcode range / city table / \"UNKNOWN\").\n27. **Persist:** `ownerRepository.save(owner)`.\n28. **Side-effect:** `ownerAuditLogger.ownerCreated(owner)` \u2014 writes id/customerCode/registrationDate to the `AUDIT` log. (No email/notification/event publishing anywhere.)\n\n## Stage D \u2014 On flush / response\n29. **Entity-level constraints** on `Owner`/`Person` are re-checked by Hibernate on flush: `firstName`/`lastName`/`address`/`city` `@NotEmpty`, `telephone` `@Pattern(\"^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")`.\n30. Controller re-maps the saved entity to `OwnerDto` (computing read-only derived fields), sets the `Location` header, returns **201 Created**.\n\n**No entity lifecycle callbacks** (`@PrePersist`/`@PostPersist`/`@EntityListeners`) exist. The only cross-cutting aspect is `CallMonitoringAspect`, which advises `@Repository` beans (JMX timing) \u2014 not a validation or business side-effect.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the household-duplicate check (#18) is silently skipped when `postcode` is null, and the disposable-email and postcode-for-city checks return HTTP 400 while the other business rules return 409/429 \u2014 a client can't distinguish \"bad input\" from \"capacity/duplicate\" purely by status class."
